"""EvoMu T-6 real-client & dual-client bridge journey harness.

Usage (as invoked by final_gate.py):
    tools/client-harness/run_journeys --out DIR --journeys FILE

Supports:
  - Spawning a local `eve-server` instance (or attaching to an existing `--bridge-port`) and capturing `<out>/server.log`.
  - Driving two concurrent client sessions (`client_1.log`, `client_2.log`) via `client-bridge/evomu_bridge.py`.
  - Detecting the real V24.01 client bundle (`~/Library/Application Support/EVE Online/SharedCache/tq/EVE.app`).
  - Enforcing the `final_gate.py` log hygiene scan (`UnimplementedRPC`, `panicked at`, `Traceback (most recent`, `EXCEPTION`).
  - Honest reporting: `journeys[<id>]["passed"]` is ONLY `True` when the real `EVE.app` client has executed the journey
    end-to-end against `eve-server`. Bridge-only verification is recorded under `bridge_verified` so `final_gate.py`
    never passes prematurely before native `P-6` handshake and `ESI-1` SSO launcher flows are complete.
"""

